  "verbalization": "Tiapride is implicated in the regulation of L-lactate dehydrogenase C chain through multiple indirect pathways. The evidence suggests that Tiapride acts as a target of several molecules, which in turn target the L-lactate dehydrogenase C chain. Specifically, Tiapride is linked to 6-phosphofructo-2-kinase/fructose-2,6-bisphosphatase 4, which is targeted by Isograndifoliol, and both of these are linked to the L-lactate dehydrogenase C chain. Similarly, Tiapride is also linked to Surface protein A, which is targeted by a compound that directly targets the L-lactate dehydrogenase C chain. While the exact mechanism by which Tiapride influences the L-lactate dehydrogenase C chain remains unclear, the evidence suggests a potential regulatory or inhibitory relationship, possibly through the modulation of enzyme activity or structural changes in the target protein. The integration of these pathways highlights the complexity of the relationship, with Tiapride potentially influencing the L-lactate dehydrogenase C chain through a network of molecular interactions that are not yet fully elucidated.",
